cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or the results in your research, please cite
  this repository using the metadata below. Update the author list,
  title and DOI once the manuscript is finalised and published.
type: software
title: >-
  Query-variation robustness of first-stage retrieval: a reproducible pilot
  (Vaswani)
abstract: >-
  Measures how BM25, a non-neural LSA retriever and their RRF hybrid respond
  to meaning-preserving query rewrites (misspelling, paraphrasing, naturality,
  word order) on the Vaswani/NPL collection, using pre-registered statistical
  tests and a fully reproducible pipeline.
